---
id: org.dxos.plugin.brain
name: BrainPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

The Facts layer for Composer: a per-space semantic index of RDF `Fact` tuples (subject / predicate /
object with factuality, attribution, and provenance) extracted from user content by upstream
pipelines (e.g. `plugin-inbox`'s `EnrichMailbox` over a mailbox feed).

The facts live in the space's memory (`MemoryService` from `@dxos/echo-memory`), which the client services host
runs and persists; the plugin's operations declare `MemoryService` and read and write it. For code that still
works through the `FactStore` seam of `@dxos/pipeline-rdf` (the email fact pipeline, stories), the plugin
contributes a `FactStoreRegistry` and a space-affinity `LayerSpec` providing `FactStore`, both over the same space
memory, so every reader sees what every writer wrote.

On top of the store, the plugin contributes:

- Three visible operations, `QueryFacts`, `QuerySparql` and `SummarizeSubject`, exposed to the assistant through the
  `org.dxos.skill.brain` skill. Skill instructions describe HOW to use the tools (entity-slug
  conventions, confidence filtering, iterative narrowing) — task-specific behavior lives in the
  operations themselves.
- A `FactsCompanion` surface rendering the plugin's `FactViewer` component over the
  space's facts as a companion to article subjects, with an entity/predicate filter and an empty
  state when no facts relate to the subject.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`   |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`   |

## Types

```mdl
type Fact
  desc: |
    Defined in @dxos/pipeline-rdf (not re-declared here). An attributed RDF assertion:
    { id, assertion: { subject: Term, predicate, object: Term }, factuality, attribution,
    recordedAt, extractor, sourceHash }. Terms are { entity, label? } | { literal }.
```

```mdl
type SemanticQueryInput
  desc: |
    The structured (browser-safe) query surface over the triple store. Mirrors
    SemanticQuery from @dxos/pipeline-rdf; raw SPARQL goes through op:querySparql instead.
  fields:
    subjectEntity?: string     # Entity slug the fact's subject must match
    predicate?: string         # Exact predicate string
    entity?: string            # Entity slug appearing as subject OR object
    source?: string            # Source DXN the fact was extracted from
    minConfidence?: number     # 0..1 lower bound on factuality confidence
    limit?: number             # Maximum facts returned (default 50)
    offset?: number            # Matching facts to skip, for windowed reads (default 0)
```

```mdl
type CompactFact
  desc: |
    LLM-facing rendering of a Fact: one line per fact, sized for tool-result context.
    Factuality is the FactBank code (CT+, PR-, ...); date is recordedAt (YYYY-MM-DD).
  fields:
    id: string
    subject: string            # Display label (or slug) of the subject term
    predicate: string
    object: string             # Display label (or slug) / literal of the object term
    factuality: string
    confidence?: number
    date: string
    source: string             # Source DXN
```

```mdl
type SummaryResult
  desc: Output of SummarizeSubject.
  fields:
    summary: string            # Grounded prose summary citing fact ids
    factCount: number          # Number of facts the summary drew from
```

```mdl
type AgentTrim
  desc: |
    How every fact tool bounds what it returns to the model: at most 50 rows and 500
    characters per value. When anything is cut, the response carries a `note` saying the
    output was truncated ("Output truncated: showing N of M rows.") and that the model must
    read the rest in windows with LIMIT/OFFSET (limit/offset for QueryFacts); a SPARQL query
    without a LIMIT is also told to add one.
  fields:
    note?: string              # Present only when rows or values were cut
```

```mdl
type FactStoreRegistry
  desc: |
    Contributed capability (BrainCapabilities.FactStoreRegistry), once the client is initialized. Each space's
    memory (client.memory) as a FactStore; subscribe fires whenever the space's store applies a batch.
  fields:
    forSpace: (spaceId) => FactStoreApi
    layerFor: (spaceId) => Layer<FactStore>
    subscribe: (spaceId, listener) => () => void
```

## Operations

```mdl
op queryFacts
  key: org.dxos.operation.brain.queryFacts
  desc: |
    Runs a structured SemanticQuery against the space memory and returns compact
    facts for LLM consumption. Visible; listed as a tool of the brain skill.
  input:
    query: SemanticQueryInput
  output: { facts: CompactFact[], total: number, note?: string }
  requires: [MemoryService]
  effects: [memory:read]
  errors:
    MemoryError: the memory could not answer the query
  note: The output is trimmed for the model (type:AgentTrim); `total` counts every match.
```

```mdl
op querySparql
  key: org.dxos.operation.brain.querySparql
  desc: |
    Runs a raw SPARQL SELECT against the space memory and returns its solutions, each
    bound variable rendered as text (IRIs as `<iri>`, blank nodes as `_:id`, literals
    verbatim). Visible; listed as a tool of the brain skill.
  input:
    sparql: string             # A SPARQL SELECT; should carry LIMIT and OFFSET
  output: { rows: Record<string, string>[], total: number, note?: string }
  requires: [MemoryService]
  effects: [memory:read]
  errors:
    MemoryError: the query is not a SELECT (an update included) or fails to run
  note: The output is trimmed for the model (type:AgentTrim); `total` counts every solution.
```

```mdl
op summarizeSubject
  key: org.dxos.operation.brain.summarizeSubject
  desc: |
    Queries all facts mentioning the subject (as subject-entity and as object entity),
    then prompts the LLM to compose a grounded summary that cites fact ids and respects
    factuality codes (uncertain facts are hedged, negated facts stated as such).
    Visible; listed as a tool of the brain skill.
  input:
    subject: string            # Entity slug or label (normalized to slug before query)
    focus?: string             # Optional angle, e.g. "commitments", "recent activity"
  output: SummaryResult
  requires: [MemoryService, AiService]
  effects: [memory:read, llm]
  errors:
    MemoryError: the memory could not answer the query
  note: Returns { summary: '', factCount: 0 } when no facts match; never invents content.
```

## Components

```mdl
component FactsCompanion
  desc: |
    Companion surface over an article subject rendering the space's facts via the FactViewer
    component (src/components/FactViewer, exported via ./components).
    Facts are read from the space's memory (client.memory), refreshed whenever its store applies a batch. v0 shows
    all space facts (the memory is per-space, matching its granularity) with FactViewer's
    text filter; subject-scoped filtering by source DXN is roadmap.
  props:
    subject: Obj.Any           # The companioned ECHO object
  state:
    facts: Fact[]              # Loaded from the store; refreshed on store writes
    filter: string             # Entity/predicate text filter (FactViewer built-in)
  slots: {}
  emits: {}
```

```mdl
component MemoryArticle
  desc: |
    The space's memory, opened from Memory under the space's settings: its fact store imported from or
    exported to TriG, a SPARQL editor, and every SPARQL query run against the store, an agent's included,
    shown live with its results as it runs.
  state:
    statements: number          # Statements across the store's named graphs; refreshed on store writes
    log: SparqlQueryRecord[]    # The registry's query log for the space, newest last
    pinned?: number             # The query the viewer picked; unset follows the newest
  actions:
    import: File -> void        # Reads a .trig/.ttl file into the store
    export: () -> void          # Downloads the store as memory-<space>.trig
    run: string -> void         # Runs a SELECT; its result arrives through the log
  layout: |
    [n statements | Import TriG | Export TriG | status]
    [SPARQL editor ............................ Run]
    [#7 #6 #5 …  (query history, newest first)     ]
    [Live query #7 · 12 rows
     SELECT …
     ?p        ?n
     uses      1204 ...                            ]
```

```mdl
component PipelineCompanion
  desc: |
    The run that filled the space's memory, as the memory records it (a JSON state in the `pipeline` graph,
    written beside the facts by `facts-cli trig`): a diagram of its sources with their first and last message,
    its stages in order, the facts written and the model each stage called with its calls and cost, drawn on a
    read-only canvas (`Scene2DView`); then the run's time, counters and cost, and its busiest channels with
    their cursor.
  state:
    pipelines: Pipeline.State[]   # Every run the store records, newest first; refreshed on store writes
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Facts in the space's memory
  uses: [FactStoreRegistry]

  req F-1.1:
    when: an operation of this plugin runs with a space context
    then: it reads and writes the space's MemoryService, which the client services host runs, so its facts persist
          and every page sees them

  req F-1.2:
    when: an operation declaring FactStore runs with a space context
    then: the plugin's LayerSpec gives it a FactStore over the space's memory

  req F-1.3:
    when: the client is initialized
    then: a FactStoreRegistry is contributed whose stores are the space memories, and whose subscribe fires on every
          batch the space's store applies
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Assistant access via the brain skill

  req F-2.1:
    when: the plugin activates
    then: the org.dxos.skill.brain skill is contributed with tools QueryFacts,
          QuerySparql and SummarizeSubject

  req F-2.2:
    when: the skill instructions are rendered
    then: they describe tool usage only (slug conventions, confidence filtering,
          iterative narrowing); no task-specific recipes

  req F-2.3:
    when: the assistant invokes QueryFacts
    then: results are compact single-line facts bounded by limit (default 50)

  req F-2.4:
    when: the assistant invokes QuerySparql with a SELECT
    then: the solutions are returned as rows of text; any other query form is refused
          with SemanticIndexError and the store is unchanged

  req F-2.5:
    when: a fact tool's result exceeds 50 rows or a value exceeds 500 characters
    then: the response is trimmed and carries a note telling the model the output was
          cut and to read the rest in windows with LIMIT/OFFSET (type:AgentTrim)
```

```mdl
feat F-3: FactViewer companion surface
  uses: [FactsCompanion]

  req F-3.1:
    when: an article subject is companioned in a space with a FactStore
    then: the FactsCompanion surface is available and renders FactViewer over the
          space's facts

  req F-3.2:
    when: the space store has no facts
    then: an empty state is shown (no error)
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Consumers resolve FactStore through the seam

  req F-4.1:
    when: plugin-inbox's EnrichMailbox indexes a mailbox feed
    then: facts land in the store this plugin provides for that space (no
          plugin-inbox → plugin-brain package dependency)

  req F-4.2:
    when: plugin-inbox's GenerateReply drafts a reply
    then: it queries the same per-space store for facts about the message's
          participants
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Memory view, TriG transfer and live queries
  uses: [MemoryArticle, FactStoreRegistry]

  req F-5.1:
    when: a space's settings are opened
    then: they list Memory, which opens the MemoryArticle over that space's store

  req F-5.2:
    when: a TriG (or Turtle) file is imported
    then: its quads are added to the space's store, the statement count updates, and the facts
          it holds answer QueryFacts and QuerySparql like facts the store extracted itself

  req F-5.3:
    when: Export TriG is clicked
    then: the store's statements, their graph metadata and its ontology download as one TriG
          document that imports into an empty store as the same facts

  req F-5.4:
    when: an agent runs QuerySparql (or a SELECT is run from the view)
    then: the query appears in the view as it starts, marked running, and its row count and first
          rows replace the marker when it ends
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Pipeline state beside the memory
  uses: [PipelineCompanion]

  req F-6.1:
    when: a crawl's facts are exported as TriG where its crawl.db and trace.jsonl lie
    then: the export carries the run's state: each channel's cursor, item count and first and last message,
          each stage's model calls, tokens and catalog cost, the run's start and end, and the facts written

  req F-6.2:
    when: the Pipeline panel is opened over a memory holding a run's state
    then: it draws the run as a diagram of channels, stages, model and facts, and lists its time, counters,
          cost and busiest channels in human-readable form
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Registry instance identity
  given: a FactStoreRegistry
  when: forSpace('a') is called twice and forSpace('b') once
  then:
    - both 'a' calls return the same instance
    - 'b' returns a distinct instance
    - layerFor('a') provides the instance forSpace('a') returned
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: QueryFacts returns matching facts
  given: a memory FactStore seeded with facts about alice (subject) and acme (object)
  when: QueryFacts runs with { entity: 'alice' } and with { minConfidence: 0.9 }
  then:
    - the entity query returns facts where alice is subject or object
    - the confidence query excludes facts below the bound
    - results are CompactFact-shaped and bounded by limit
```

```mdl
scenario T-6: QuerySparql runs raw SELECTs and trims for the model
  given: a memory FactStore seeded with facts
  when: QuerySparql runs a SELECT, an update, and a SELECT with more than 50 solutions
  then:
    - the SELECT returns its solutions as text rows
    - the update fails with SemanticIndexError and every fact remains
    - the large result returns 50 rows with a truncation note; without a LIMIT the note
      says to add one
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: SummarizeSubject grounds on facts
  given: a memory FactStore seeded with facts about a person, and a memoized LLM
  when: SummarizeSubject runs with that subject
  then:
    - factCount equals the number of matched facts
    - the summary cites at least one fact id
    - with an unknown subject: summary is empty and factCount is 0
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: FactsCompanion rendering
  given: a space store with facts (storybook)
  when: FactsCompanion renders over a subject
  then:
    - FactViewer shows the facts grouped by subject
    - with an empty store the empty state renders
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: Enrich → query integration (lives in plugin-inbox)
  given: a mailbox feed with messages and the brain-provided store
  when: EnrichMailbox runs, then QueryFacts for a participant entity
  then: facts extracted from the messages are returned
```

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

This plugin has no create operation of its own — facts land in the store via upstream pipelines
(`plugin-inbox`'s `EnrichMailbox`), never through a user gesture this plugin owns — so there is
nothing for `before`/`test` to create and nothing for `after` to undo. `queryFacts` and
`summarizeSubject` are both agent-invocable read operations (`op@1.1`, keys below).

```mdl
test QA-1: Query and summarize facts already in the store
  desc: The plugin's own surface — QueryFacts and SummarizeSubject against a pre-populated FactStore.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-2.1, F-2.3, F-3.1, T-2, T-3]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open whose FactStore already holds facts about entity "alice-smith" —
      seeded by a prior plugin-inbox EnrichMailbox run (see F-4.1); this plugin has no operation
      that creates a fact itself
  steps:
    - name: Query facts about the entity
      do: (no direct UI for a structured query — this is the assistant path; a human instead opens
        the FactsCompanion below and types "alice-smith" into its filter)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.brain.queryFacts { entity: "alice-smith" }
      capture: queried
      expect: every returned fact has "alice-smith" as its subject or object entity, bounded by
        the default limit of 50
      assert: return $result.facts.length > 0 && $result.facts.every((f) => f.subject.includes('alice') || f.object.includes('alice'));
    - name: Summarize the entity
      do: (assistant path only — ask the assistant "summarize alice-smith")
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.brain.summarizeSubject { subject: "alice-smith" }
      expect: a grounded summary is returned that cites at least one fact id, with factCount > 0
      assert: return $result.factCount > 0 && $result.summary.length > 0;
    - name: Open the FactsCompanion
      do: Companion an object touched by the seeded facts (e.g. the enriched mailbox message) and
        open its Facts companion panel.
      expect: FactViewer lists the space's facts, filterable by entity/predicate text
      note: NO `invoke` — FactsCompanion is a read-only React surface, not backed by an operation.
```

```mdl
test QA-2: An agent turns a community's memory into sheets with charts, a deck and a summary
  desc: Import the Cloudflare Developers Discord's facts as TriG, then ask the Composer assistant what its memory says, without telling it which skills to use; the Memory view shows each query as the agent runs it.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-5.1, F-5.2, F-5.4, F-2.4]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists, with a model the assistant can reach
    - a TriG export of a crawl's fact store (`moon run plugin-discord:facts -- trig <out.trig> --facts <facts.db>`)
  steps:
    - name: Import the community's memory
      do: Open the space's settings, open Memory, click Import TriG and pick the export.
      expect: the toolbar reports the quads imported and the statement count matches the export
    - name: Ask the agent what its memory says
      do: Open a chat beside Memory and ask for the five most interesting things about the community, each as a sheet with a chart, then a presentation and a summary.
      expect: Memory shows the agent's SPARQL queries one after another, each with its rows, as the agent explores
    - name: Read what it made
      do: Open the sheets, the presentation and the document the agent created.
      expect: each sheet holds the rows a query returned and a chart of them; the deck and the summary describe the same five findings
      note: The findings are the model's; nothing in the flow names them.
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: An agent tool runs a raw SPARQL query against the fact store, and the fact tools' responses to the agent are trimmed with a note that makes the model use LIMIT and windowed reads.
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [querySparql, queryFacts, AgentTrim, F-2.4, F-2.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: `QuerySparql` accepts only a SELECT, renders each bound term as text, and fails with `SemanticIndexError` on anything else. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [querySparql, F-2.4]
  why: The store's `rows` already refuses updates with that error, so the tool reads and never writes; text terms keep rows small and pasteable back into SPARQL.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Every fact tool returns at most 50 rows and 500 characters per value; a cut response carries a note naming N of M rows and how to page, and QueryFacts gains `offset` and `total` so it pages the same way. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-14
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [AgentTrim, queryFacts, F-2.5]
  why: 50 rows matches QueryFacts' default limit and keeps one tool result within a few thousand tokens.
  rejected:
    - A total character budget alone: it cuts rows unpredictably and gives the model no window to resume from.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A space's memory moves in and out of Composer as TriG, from a Memory view under the space's settings that also shows every SPARQL query run against the store, live.
  date: 2026-11-17
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [MemoryArticle, F-5]
  why: TriG is Turtle with named graphs, which a fact needs since each fact is a graph; plain Turtle would drop the graph and with it the fact's provenance.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: A memory imported as TriG carries the state of the run that produced it, and a Pipeline panel draws it as a canvas diagram with the run's counters, cost, time, models and cursors. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-11-17
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [PipelineCompanion, F-6]
  why: Keeping the state in the store means the panel reads one source, the memory, whether the run was a local crawl or Composer's own.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: Brain's facts live in the space's MemoryService, which replaces the per-tab in-memory FactStore registry.
  date: 2026-11-17
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1, queryFacts, querySparql, summarizeSubject, FactsCompanion]
```

```mdl
decision D-7: The operations declare MemoryService and fail with MemoryError; FactStoreRegistry and the FactStore LayerSpec stay, both over the space memory, for the email pipeline and the stories that read through a FactStore. Fills in [D-6].
  date: 2026-11-17
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1, FactStoreRegistry, queryFacts, querySparql, summarizeSubject]
  supersedes: D-2
  why: The registry's readers (the facts companion's tests, nine story modules) need no change when its stores are the memory, and one memory means a story's reads see what operations wrote.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: The Memory view's query log is kept per space memory, and `QuerySparql` records each query it runs in it, so an agent's queries still show live now that the operation reads MemoryService rather than a logged FactStore. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-11-17
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [MemoryArticle, querySparql, FactStoreRegistry]
  why: An operation sees only the space's MemoryService, which the client hands out once per space, so that instance is the key that joins the agent's queries to the view.
```


Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap        # name[?]: TypeExpr  (# inline comment)
    literals?: UnionList     # a | b | c
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap            # external inputs (immutable inside component)
    state?: FieldMap            # internal reactive state
    slots?: FieldMap            # named ReactNode injection points
    actions?: ActionMap         # methods the component exposes or handles
    emits?: EventMap            # events the component raises to its parent
    layout?: CodeBlock          # ASCII sketch of visual structure (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap            # named input parameters
    output?: TypeExpr           # return type
    errors?: ErrorMap           # name: Prose  (when this error occurs)
    effects?: EffectList        # echo:read | echo:write | http | fs | ...
    requires?: ServiceList      # injected service dependencies
    note?: Prose                # implementation guidance (non-normative)
```
